From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrisohearn <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:54:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/93] spi: apple-qspi: admit the K114s NVRAM, fail-closed on
 its flash ID

The K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro, Mac17,13) has the J716s's
QSPI controller at 0x505118000 and, in its macOS 27.2 (26B8125) ADT, the
same NVRAM at /arm-io/qspi/spinor/anvram: 0x700000, 0xc0000 bytes, twelve
64 KiB banks. Add its row beside the J716s's so root can opt in to the
same bounded and verified writes.

The flash ID is the J716s's GigaDevice part (0xc88317) by assumption; it
has not been read on a K114s. If the part differs, the existing JEDEC
check refuses every write before WREN, so a first boot can only read and
report the real ID. No block-protect bit is tolerated (bp_ok 0).

tools/asahi/qspi-nvram-tests.py passes unchanged with the row added.
Not yet run on the hardware.
---
 drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
index a0f0b05cf3b..4e1995fe9de 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
@@ -160,6 +160,16 @@ static const struct apple_qspi_board apple_qspi_boards[] = {
 	 */
 	{ "apple,t6050-qspi", "apple,j716s", 0x505118000ULL,
 	  0x700000, 0xc0000, APPLE_QSPI_JEDEC_GD_8M, 0 },
+	/*
+	 * K114s (T6050, MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro): the ADT gives the
+	 * same controller aperture and the same NVRAM, 12 banks of 64 KiB at
+	 * 0x700000 (/arm-io/qspi/spinor/anvram). The flash ID is assumed to be
+	 * the J716s's GigaDevice part and is not yet confirmed on a K114s: a
+	 * different ID refuses every write before WREN, so the first boot can
+	 * only read. No block-protect bit is tolerated.
+	 */
+	{ "apple,t6050-qspi", "apple,k114s", 0x505118000ULL,
+	  0x700000, 0xc0000, APPLE_QSPI_JEDEC_GD_8M, 0 },
 };
 
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(apple_qspi_policy_lock);
